  "bio": {
    "eyebrow": "About Dr Hanna",
    "heading_lead": "Meet",
    "heading_warm": "Dr Hanna.",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Dr Mina Hanna is an independent Consultant Specialist GP (ABN: 98 294 983 063) (MED0001602932) consulting at the Bangor centre.",
      "Dr Mina Hanna graduated from the University of New South Wales with an honours degree. After completing his internship and residency in Bankstown and Campbelltown Hospitals, he underwent specialist physician training in internal medicine at Concord and Nepean Hospitals before entering into family medicine.",
      "Dr Mina enjoys teaching medical students and junior doctors. He has held various academic appointments and has received awards, including Registrar Teacher of the Year. In addition to English, Dr Mina also speaks Arabic. He enjoys spending time with his family and friends and is keenly involved in various Church services and exploring theology and philosophy.",
      "Dr Mina can speak fluent Arabic in addition to English."
    ]
  },
